      <marc:subfield code="a">Mike Krzyzewski, with an unquestioned track record as the head coach at Duke, was chosen to lead the U.S. basketball team for the 2008 Beijing Olympics. His challenge was to adapt the coaching methods that worked with college kids to a team of NBA superstars. The naysayers felt no one could rein in the egos of millionaire NBA stars, but in his telling of the tale, the egos weren&apos;t an issue. To a man, the players sublimated their games to the needs of the team. Krzyzewski relates his team-building techniques, offers numerous anecdotes about the players, and provides insightful commentary on the key games</marc:subfield>
